MEMBERSHIP ORACLE
INPUT : prime p; modulus kind in {X^2+1, X^2+X+1}
OUTPUT: whether p can divide the modulus for some input
1. if kind = X^2+1     then return (p = 2) or (p mod 4 = 1)
2. if kind = X^2+X+1   then return (p = 3) or (p mod 3 = 1)

AUDIT
INPUT : window bound R, prime bound P
3. observed <- {}
4. for N = 1 to R-1 do
5.     observed <- observed  U  PRIME-FACTORS(value(N))
6. violations <- { p in observed : not ORACLE(p) }
7. missing    <- { p < P prime : ORACLE(p) and p not in observed }
8. return (|observed|, violations, missing)   // violations must be empty
